{
  "id": "08049_uyamuya",
  "headword": "うやむや",
  "reading": "うやむや",
  "part_of_speech": "na-adjective",
  "gloss": "vague; ambiguous; inconclusive",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "vague; ambiguous; hazy; inconclusive",
      "explanation": "a state where something is left unclear, unresolved, or deliberately obscured"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "08049_uyamuya_ex1",
      "japanese": "{問題|もんだい}がうやむやになった。",
      "english": "The problem was left unresolved.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08049_uyamuya_ex2",
      "japanese": "{責任|せきにん}をうやむやにする。",
      "english": "To avoid clearly assigning responsibility.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08049_uyamuya_ex3",
      "japanese": "{話|はなし}をうやむやにしないでください。",
      "english": "Please don't leave things vague.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\nFrom {有耶無耶|うやむや} - literally \"is it there or is it not there,\" expressing uncertainty.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- うやむやになる (to become vague/unclear)\n- うやむやにする (to make something vague, to obscure)\n- うやむやな{返事|へんじ} (vague answer)\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used with negative connotation, implying that something was deliberately left unclear to avoid accountability or difficult conclusions.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- あやふや (uncertain, unreliable)\n- {曖昧|あいまい} (ambiguous)\n- {不明瞭|ふめいりょう} (unclear)",
